WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.900
We have some stunning new polling numbers
which should serve to do nothing.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:11.240
And other than to reinforce the opportunity
that we have to remove Donald Trump in November

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.999
if we all get out and vote.

00:00:13.999 --> 00:00:19.510
This is a stunning new poll out of North Carolina,
which puts Joe Biden seven points ahead of

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:20.650
Donald Trump.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.460
This is not a Democratic leaning poll.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.470
In fact, it gives Biden a bigger advantage
over Trump than two recent left leaning polls

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:33.460
from Change Research and Peepee, which respectively
have Biden plus one and plus four.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:37.630
This poll of registered voters says Biden
is winning by seven.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:42.270
And as we approach Election Day, I've said
before we will see a transition from registered

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:46.750
voter models being used in polling to likely
voter models.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:51.899
And what's interesting is that the admittedly
Democratic leaning Change Research poll is

00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:56.430
a likely voter model and may actually be more
accurate in Joe Biden's lead in North Carolina.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:02.070
If indeed it exists maybe significantly smaller
than the seven points that we have most recently

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.070
seen.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:06.280
On average, Joe Biden's lead in North Carolina
is now three.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:12.230
Now, as a reminder, in 2016, Donald Trump
won North Carolina by a little more than three

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.440
and a half points.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.979
And certainly losing North Carolina would
be a really bad signal for Donald Trump and

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:24.060
one that, you know, depending on the numbers
we might know about relatively early on November

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.060
3rd.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.299
North Carolina being on the East Coast, voting
closes earlier than a lot of other states.

00:01:29.299 --> 00:01:34.180
And if it's not even close in North Carolina,
we might know that very early in the evening.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:38.140
And that would be an important signal about
the way the election is going to go.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:43.060
Now, just as important out of North Carolina,
based on what we were talking about yesterday,

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:48.420
the Democratic Senate candidate, Cal Cunningham,
has a nine point lead in the same poll over

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.340
the incumbent Republican Senator Thom Tillis.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.170
This would be a huge victory.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:56.910
This would be tremendous in the context of
Democrats maybe taking the Senate, as we were

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.520
discussing yesterday.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:05.229
So now it's time for a word of caution that
is different than my warning from earlier

00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:07.659
about everybody has to vote and Trump can
win.

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:09.819
That was a general sort of word of caution.

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:12.450
Now, I want to be a little more specific.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:18.560
We see Joe Biden winning on average by almost
eight points in Florida, six in Wisconsin,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.840
eight in Michigan, seven in Pennsylvania,
four in Arizona.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.410
This should remind us that we can't underestimate
Donald Trump.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:33.640
Remember that in 2018, a record number of
Republicans voted in the midterms.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:39.000
And because Democrats also had record turnout,
we picked up a bunch of seats in the House.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:47.960
So if Democrats in 2020 and left leaning independents
merely match prior turnout, we could easily

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:48.960
lose.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:54.690
So as we see these numbers, as important as
they are, as signals about an opportunity

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:58.800
to not only defeat Donald Trump and maybe
take the Senate and grow the majority in the

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:05.459
House, we should be reminded that when Republicans
see this polling, they may become more vote

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:07.110
motivated to vote.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:12.530
Some may write these polls office fake polls,
but not all of them, meaning we need to not

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:17.270
just match but exceed our biggest ever turnout.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:22.030
And I believe we need to dramatically exceed
it as we approach November.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:27.909
If the administration is indeed lying about
rhinovirus numbers, if you see successful

00:03:27.909 --> 00:03:34.459
efforts to restrict absentee voting by mail,
close polling places, federal paramilitary

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:38.200
troops intimidating voters like if you add
all of this stuff up a little bit.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.200
A little bit.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.200
A little bit.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.200
Death of a thousand cuts.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:46.220
We need not just to exceed prior turnout,
but we need to dramatically exceed prior turnout

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:50.640
in order to not allow this to be a missed
opportunity.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.010
Maybe Trump won't get out the vote.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.010
Great.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.110
We benefit, OK?

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:57.280
Maybe Trump won't be able to suppress the
vote because judges are a quote.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.280
You.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.280
Who knows.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.280
Will prevent fantastic.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.280
Whatever.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.280
We can't control that.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:07.670
And so what we can do is vote ourselves and
get out the vote and make sure that we are

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:12.430
so overwhelming turnout that the dirty tricks
can't work.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.680
There will be dirty tricks.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.329
We're already seeing them.

00:04:16.329 --> 00:04:18.379
There's no question that there will be dirty
tricks.

00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:21.099
The question is, will they matter?

00:04:21.099 --> 00:04:24.629
Because if we really boost turnout in a way
that typically nobody does.

00:04:24.629 --> 00:04:26.800
Everybody talks about boosting turnout and
rarely does it.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.410
Does it really happen to the.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:32.610
Three that I'm thinking about and many people
are thinking about, only if we do that can

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:34.639
we say the dirty tricks won't work.

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:37.069
The dirty tricks won't be enough.

00:04:37.069 --> 00:04:38.800
And that's exactly what we need to hope for.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.069
Now, in the meantime, Donald Trump.

00:04:41.069 --> 00:04:42.940
I don't know if this is a good strategy.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:44.639
I'll talk about it.

00:04:44.639 --> 00:04:47.819
Donald Trump is just insisting the polls are
fake.

00:04:47.819 --> 00:04:50.879
And that may actually be a counterproductive
strategy for him.

00:04:50.879 --> 00:05:21.309
I'm going 
to

